  "EU AI Act: What Actually Applies on 2 August 2026": "EU AI Act: What Actually Applies on 2 August 2026",
  "Educational demo: HMAC-SHA256 with a shared secret, showing request-bound, expiring, verifiable license tokens. Production tokens should be signed asymmetrically, with the publisher’s public key discoverable under /.well-known/.": "Fakatātā ako: HMAC-SHA256 ʻaki ha meʻa fakapulipuli fevahevaheʻaki, ʻo fakahā ai ha ngaahi token laiseni fehoanaki mo e kole, ʻoku ʻosi taimi, pea lava ke sivi. Ko e ngaahi token moʻoni ʻoku totonu ke fakamoʻoniʻi ʻi ha founga taʻe tatau, ʻaki ha kī fakalūkufua ʻo e tokotaha pulusi ʻe lava ke ʻilo ʻi lalo ʻi he /.well-known/.",
  "Eight more /topics entries, this time researched by an AI agent rather than curated by hand — same rule as before: every source fetched and confirmed live, summaries an original paraphrase, before anything gets added. 14 entries total.": "Ko e toe ngaahi kupu ʻe valu ki he /topics, ko e taimi ni naʻe fakatotolo ʻe ha ʻeiseni AI kae ʻikai fili ʻaki ha nima — tatau pē ʻa e lao muʻa: ko e tupuʻanga kotoa pē kuo toʻo mai pea fakamoʻoniʻi ʻoku kei moʻui, ko e ngaahi fakanounou ko ha toe tohi tefito, kimuʻa pea tānaki ha meʻa. ʻOku fakakātoa ki he kupu ʻe 14.",
