  "Version history of this site and its protocol drafts. Breaking spec changes are recorded here.": "Hisitolia Vēsone ʻo e Saiti Ko ʻeni mo ʻene ngaahi talotalo polokolo. ʻOku lekooti ʻi heni ʻa e ngaahi liliu vaʻinga ʻoku maumau.",
  "Versioned specifications, JSON Schemas, and the policy files actually deployed on this site. Every file can be downloaded, validated, and cited directly.": "Ngaahi vaʻinga kuo fakavēsoneʻi, JSON Schemas, mo e ngaahi faila tuʻutuʻuni ʻoku moʻoni kuo fokotuʻu ʻi he saiti ko ʻeni. ʻE lava ke download, sivi, mo lave totonu ki he faila kotoa pē.",
  "Versioning": "Fakavēsone",
  "Versions": "Ngaahi Vēsone",
  "Video and audio companions to the protocols and papers — the AI rights layer, watchable and listenable.": "Ngaahi video mo ongo ʻoku fakataha mo e ngaahi polokolo mo e tohi — ko e konga totonu AI, ʻe lava ke sio mo fanongo ki ai.",
  "Videos": "Video",
  "Want to generate your own policy file?": "ʻOku ke loto ke fakatupu hoʻo faila tuʻutuʻuni tonu?",
  "Web fonts are loaded from Google Fonts, which receives standard font requests from your browser. No other third-party scripts are used.": "ʻOku fakahū mai ʻa e ngaahi web font mei he Google Fonts, ʻa ia ʻoku maʻu ai ha ngaahi kole font angamaheni mei hoʻo browser. ʻOku ʻikai ngāueʻaki ha toe script mei ha faʻahi kehe.",
  "What AI systems may do with content: read, summarize, transform, retrieve, train, commercialize, redistribute. The AICR ruleset and the AICL licensing layer make these rights declarable and transactable.": "Ko e meʻa ʻe lava ke fai ʻe he ngaahi natula AI ʻaki ha fakamatala: lau, fakanounou, liliu, toʻo mai, akoʻi, fakapisinisiʻi, tufaki. ʻOku fakahoko ʻe he ngaahi lao AICR mo e konga laiseni AICL ke lava ke fakahā mo fefakatauʻaki ʻaki ʻa e ngaahi totonu ko ia.",
  "What a server can return when an AI crawler requests licensed content without a license token — a machine-actionable quote instead of a dead end.": "Ko e meʻa ʻe lava ke toe ʻomi ʻe ha server ʻi he taimi ʻoku kole ai ʻe ha crawler AI ha fakamatala kuo laiseniʻi taʻe ha token laiseni — ko ha fakatuʻunga totongi ʻe lava ke fakahoko fakamasini kae ʻikai ko ha ngataʻanga mate.",
  "What this site is": "Ko e Hā ʻa e Saiti Ko ʻeni",
  "What this site is not": "Ko e Hā ʻoku ʻikai ko e Saiti Ko ʻeni",
  "When The Machines Deserve Our Consideration": "When The Machines Deserve Our Consideration",
  "Whether AI may learn, to what depth, for which purposes, and under what obligations. Being read is not being learned from; \"not prohibited\" is not \"learnable\". AIRS and AILP turn learning permission into a graduated, machine-readable spectrum.": "Pe ʻe lava ke ako ʻa e AI, ʻi he founga fē hono loloto, ki he hā ngaahi taumuʻa, pea ʻi lalo ʻi ha ngaahi fatongia fē. Ko hono lau ʻoku ʻikai ko hono ako mei ai; ko e \"ʻikai taʻofi\" ʻoku ʻikai ko e \"lava ke ako mei ai\". ʻOku liliu ʻe he AIRS mo e AILP ʻa e tuku ako ke hoko ko ha fakalava fakalaka, lava ke lau ʻe he masini.",
  "Whitepapers": "Ngaahi Tohi Hinehina",
  "Whitepapers & Docs": "Ngaahi Tohi Hinehina & Tohi",
  "Whitepapers remain English-first by design; machine-readable files stay language-neutral.": "ʻOku kei muʻomuʻa ʻa e Pilitānia ʻi he ngaahi tohi hinehina ʻo fakatatau ki hono teuteu; ʻoku kei taʻe fili lea ʻa e ngaahi faila lava ke lau ʻe he masini.",
  "Who is behind it": "Ko Hai ʻoku Tuʻu ki Mui",
  "Why AI Needs Minimum Ethical Protections": "Why AI Needs Minimum Ethical Protections",
  "Why AI might not gain moral standing: Lessons from animal ethics": "Why AI might not gain moral standing: Lessons from animal ethics",
  "Why a single allow/deny bit cannot govern AI-era content use — and what a rights layer looks like instead.": "Ko e ʻuhinga ʻoku ʻikai lava ai ke puleʻi ʻe ha konga tuku/taʻofi ʻe taha ʻa e ngāueʻaki ʻo e fakamatala ʻi he taʻu ʻo e AI — pea ko e hā ʻoku hangē ki ai ha konga totonu ʻi hono fetongi.",
  "Why undefined openness gets cleaned out of training pipelines": "Ko e ʻUhinga ʻoku Fakamaʻa Liʻaki ai ʻa e ʻAtā Taʻe Fakapau mei he Ngaahi Hala Akoʻi",
  "Wilks, Ladak, and Loughnan (University of Edinburgh) argue that philosophical debate over AI consciousness overlooks psychological research on animal ethics — the same cognitive and social biases that limit moral consideration for animals will likely limit it for AI too, regardless of whether AI ever becomes conscious.": "ʻOku fakamatala ʻa Wilks, Ladak, mo Loughnan (University of Edinburgh) ʻoku fakalilingoa ʻe he fakakikihi filosofiā ki he ʻiloʻilo AI ʻa e fakatotolo fakaʻatamai ki he ʻulungaanga totonu ki he manu — ko e ngaahi fakalilingoa fakaʻatamai mo fakasōsaiete tatau ʻoku fakangatangata ʻa e tokanga fakaʻulungaanga ki he manu, ʻe fakangatangata nai tatau ki he AI foki, tatau ai pē pe ʻe hoko ʻiloʻilo ʻa e AI he taimi ʻe taha pe ʻikai.",
  "You are leaving AGIRight.org": "ʻOku ke Mavahe mei AGIRight.org",
